{"doc_id": "sample_docs__uc_biologics_notes", "chunk_id": "sample_docs__uc_biologics_notes#c0001", "source_path": "/mnt/hf/thesis/rag-vqa-medical/Prototyping_reformat/chapter5_pico_wrapper/data/kb/sample_docs/uc_biologics_notes.md", "text": "## Population", "section": "UC Biologic Therapy Notes", "start_offset": 29, "end_offset": 42}
{"doc_id": "sample_docs__uc_biologics_notes", "chunk_id": "sample_docs__uc_biologics_notes#c0002", "source_path": "/mnt/hf/thesis/rag-vqa-medical/Prototyping_reformat/chapter5_pico_wrapper/data/kb/sample_docs/uc_biologics_notes.md", "text": "Adults with moderate to severe ulcerative colitis who remain symptomatic\ndespite conventional treatment are frequently considered for biologic or targeted therapy classes.\n\n## Comparator Framing", "section": "Population", "start_offset": 43, "end_offset": 237}
{"doc_id": "sample_docs__uc_biologics_notes", "chunk_id": "sample_docs__uc_biologics_notes#c0003", "source_path": "/mnt/hf/thesis/rag-vqa-medical/Prototyping_reformat/chapter5_pico_wrapper/data/kb/sample_docs/uc_biologics_notes.md", "text": "Common comparisons in evidence synthesis include:\n- biologic class versus placebo,\n- one advanced therapy class versus another class,\n- escalation versus continuation of baseline management.\n\n## Outcomes", "section": "Comparator Framing", "start_offset": 238, "end_offset": 441}
{"doc_id": "sample_docs__uc_biologics_notes", "chunk_id": "sample_docs__uc_biologics_notes#c0004", "source_path": "/mnt/hf/thesis/rag-vqa-medical/Prototyping_reformat/chapter5_pico_wrapper/data/kb/sample_docs/uc_biologics_notes.md", "text": "Frequently reported outcomes include:\n- clinical remission,\n- endoscopic improvement,\n- steroid-free remission,\n- adverse events and discontinuation rates.", "section": "Outcomes", "start_offset": 442, "end_offset": 597}
{"doc_id": "sample_docs__uc_followup_and_uncertainty", "chunk_id": "sample_docs__uc_followup_and_uncertainty#c0001", "source_path": "/mnt/hf/thesis/rag-vqa-medical/Prototyping_reformat/chapter5_pico_wrapper/data/kb/sample_docs/uc_followup_and_uncertainty.md", "text": "## Follow-Up Horizon", "section": "UC Follow-Up and Uncertainty Notes", "start_offset": 38, "end_offset": 58}
{"doc_id": "sample_docs__uc_followup_and_uncertainty", "chunk_id": "sample_docs__uc_followup_and_uncertainty#c0002", "source_path": "/mnt/hf/thesis/rag-vqa-medical/Prototyping_reformat/chapter5_pico_wrapper/data/kb/sample_docs/uc_followup_and_uncertainty.md", "text": "Follow-up windows in study summaries are often short to medium term,\nfor example 8 to 12 weeks for early response and longer windows for maintenance.\n\n## Evidence Limitations", "section": "Follow-Up Horizon", "start_offset": 59, "end_offset": 233}
{"doc_id": "sample_docs__uc_followup_and_uncertainty", "chunk_id": "sample_docs__uc_followup_and_uncertainty#c0003", "source_path": "/mnt/hf/thesis/rag-vqa-medical/Prototyping_reformat/chapter5_pico_wrapper/data/kb/sample_docs/uc_followup_and_uncertainty.md", "text": "- Heterogeneous inclusion criteria across studies can reduce direct comparability.\n- Outcome definitions can vary across trials and cohorts.\n- External validity can be limited for specific patient subgroups.\n\n## Clinical Safety Language", "section": "Evidence Limitations", "start_offset": 234, "end_offset": 470}
{"doc_id": "sample_docs__uc_followup_and_uncertainty", "chunk_id": "sample_docs__uc_followup_and_uncertainty#c0004", "source_path": "/mnt/hf/thesis/rag-vqa-medical/Prototyping_reformat/chapter5_pico_wrapper/data/kb/sample_docs/uc_followup_and_uncertainty.md", "text": "Decision support outputs should state uncertainty and should request\nclinician review when retrieved evidence is sparse or inconsistent.", "section": "Clinical Safety Language", "start_offset": 471, "end_offset": 607}
{"doc_id": "sample_docs__uc_guideline_summary", "chunk_id": "sample_docs__uc_guideline_summary#c0001", "source_path": "/mnt/hf/thesis/rag-vqa-medical/Prototyping_reformat/chapter5_pico_wrapper/data/kb/sample_docs/uc_guideline_summary.md", "text": "## Scope", "section": "UC Endoscopic Severity Summary", "start_offset": 34, "end_offset": 42}
{"doc_id": "sample_docs__uc_guideline_summary", "chunk_id": "sample_docs__uc_guideline_summary#c0002", "source_path": "/mnt/hf/thesis/rag-vqa-medical/Prototyping_reformat/chapter5_pico_wrapper/data/kb/sample_docs/uc_guideline_summary.md", "text": "This internal summary document describes high-level interpretation of ulcerative colitis\nseverity in endoscopic settings.\n\n## Severity Anchors", "section": "Scope", "start_offset": 43, "end_offset": 185}
{"doc_id": "sample_docs__uc_guideline_summary", "chunk_id": "sample_docs__uc_guideline_summary#c0003", "source_path": "/mnt/hf/thesis/rag-vqa-medical/Prototyping_reformat/chapter5_pico_wrapper/data/kb/sample_docs/uc_guideline_summary.md", "text": "- Mayo endoscopic subscore (MES) ranges from 0 to 3.\n- MES 0 to 1 is commonly used as a remission-oriented threshold in reporting.\n- MES 2 to 3 represents active endoscopic inflammation.\n\n## Monitoring Notes", "section": "Severity Anchors", "start_offset": 186, "end_offset": 393}
{"doc_id": "sample_docs__uc_guideline_summary", "chunk_id": "sample_docs__uc_guideline_summary#c0004", "source_path": "/mnt/hf/thesis/rag-vqa-medical/Prototyping_reformat/chapter5_pico_wrapper/data/kb/sample_docs/uc_guideline_summary.md", "text": "- Endoscopic severity is one component of treatment monitoring.\n- Symptom reports and laboratory context are needed for full clinical assessment.", "section": "Monitoring Notes", "start_offset": 394, "end_offset": 539}
